  "notes": "Cash basis. Statement lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p4). Taxes 853,459 split by the Statement of Activities general receipts (p2): Property 731,116 + Motor vehicle 37,163 + Lodging 85,180 = 853,459. Local 112,622 split by Statement of Activities: charges for services 46,207 + interest income 22,860 + miscellaneous 43,555 = 112,622; sale of assets 2,000 is other financing (p4). Intergovernmental 377,251 = operating grants 66,275 + general intergovernmental 310,976 (p2). Capital outlay 240,155 spans General, Road, ARPA, STOP and Road Equipment funds, so no single function. Beginning cash not printed separately; ending cash = total assets (cash 893,405 + restricted cash 395,473, p3); fund balances 1,213,023 -> 1,288,878 (p4). Balance sheet: governmental funds statement of assets and fund balances Total column (p3); totals equal the Statement of Net Position (p1). Detail: General Fund (sub-fund column) from its budgetary comparison schedule (p8, departments not itemized; Local 105,393 there includes sale of assets 200); Inheritance Tax, Veteran's Aid, Library, Relief/Medical (no activity) and Institutions sub-funds from the General Fund combining statement (p5); Road Fund from its budget schedule (p9; excludes sale of assets 1,800); nonmajor funds per column from the nonmajor combining statement (p6-7). General Fund transfers out 205,272 include 35,182 to the Library and Institutions sub-funds (net 170,090 on p4). Read pages 1-9 of 9"
